    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_h044"
      ],
      "explanation": "For a fixed logarithm base \\(c>0\\), \\(c\\ne1\\), the reciprocal rule gives\n\\[\n\\log\\frac18=\\log(8^{-1})=-\\log8.\n\\]\nBoth arguments are positive, and \\(\\log8\\ne0\\) because \\(8\\ne1\\). Therefore the denominator is nonzero and\n\\[\n\\frac{\\log8}{\\log(1/8)}\n=\\frac{\\log8}{-\\log8}=-1.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
      "id": "reciprocal-logarithm",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1961_AMC_12_Q06#reciprocal-logarithm",
      "title": "Use the reciprocal rule"
    }
  ],
